<mxCell id="t" value="DISTRIBUTED LOGGING (Splunk / ELK) - System Context" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1a237e" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="20" width="1580" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="subtitle" value="Multi-source ingestion → Kafka buffering → Flink stream processing → Hot/Warm/Cold tiered storage with Elasticsearch for search" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#e8eaf6;align=center;rounded=1;fontSize=13" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="150" y="65" width="1400" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="boundary" value="DISTRIBUTED LOGGING PLATFORM" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#ef6c00;strokeWidth=4;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;spacingLeft=15" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="320" y="140" width="1000" height="640" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="ingestion" value="INGESTION&#10;&#10;FluentBit/OTEL agents&#10;API Gateway&#10;Kafka buffering&#10;Batch file upload" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#bbdefb;strokeColor=#1976d2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="350" y="195" width="200" height="140" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="processing" value="PROCESSING&#10;&#10;Flink stream&#10;Validation&#10;Parsing&#10;Normalization&#10;Deduplication" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffcc80;strokeColor=#ef6c00;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="600" y="195" width="180" height="160" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="storage" value="STORAGE&#10;&#10;Hot: Cassandra+ES&#10;(0-14 days)&#10;Warm: Cassandra&#10;(14-45 days)&#10;Cold: S3 Parquet&#10;(45+ days)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#c8e6c9;strokeColor=#388e3c;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="830" y="195" width="220" height="180" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="search" value="SEARCH&#10;&#10;Full-text search&#10;Real-time tail&#10;Aggregations&#10;Dashboards" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1bee7;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1090" y="195" width="200" height="130" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="principles" value="KEY DESIGN RULES&#10;&#10;1. Kafka buffering prevents data loss: Agent → Kafka → Flink → DB. If DB goes down, Kafka holds millions of logs without loss. Kafka RF=3, acks=all, min.insync.replicas=2. Agent local buffer: 10MB disk, 24h retry. No log is dropped even if entire pipeline is down for hours.&#10;&#10;2. At-least-once delivery with deduplication: Agents retry on failure (at-least-once). Flink deduplicates using 5-min tumbling window + hash(timestamp_minute + service + message[0:100]). Catches 99% of duplicates. Better to deduplicate centrally than risk data loss.&#10;&#10;3. Hot/Warm/Cold tiered storage: 99% of queries hit last 14 days (hot tier: Cassandra SSD + Elasticsearch, 200ms latency). 14-45 days (warm: Cassandra HDD only, 1-2s). 45+ days (cold: S3 Parquet, Athena query, 10-30s). Saves 90% on storage costs vs keeping everything hot.&#10;&#10;4. Flink watermarks handle late logs: Logs arrive out-of-order (network delays, container restarts). Watermark = 5-min delay. Accepts logs up to 10 min late into correct time window. Extremely late (10+ min) → Dead Letter Queue for manual review. Without watermarks, alert windows would be wrong.&#10;&#10;5. Sampling reduces volume by 60%: DEBUG logs → 10% sampled, INFO → 50%, ERROR/FATAL → 100%. At 1M requests/sec, logging every DEBUG = 20M lines/sec = impossible to store. Sampling keeps signal (errors) while dropping noise (debug spam).&#10;&#10;6. Alerting with cooldown prevents fatigue: Alert on count thresholds (ERROR &gt; 100 in 5 min), not individual errors (would send 100 pages). Cooldown: 10 min before re-alerting same condition. Aggregation + deduplication + severity levels = actionable alerts, not spam." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#ef6c00;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="350" y="420" width="940" height="330" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="apps" value="APPLICATIONS&#10;&#10;Microservices&#10;Containers&#10;VMs&#10;K8s pods&#10;&#10;Print to stdout" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#bbdefb;strokeColor=#1976d2;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="50" y="230" width="200" height="155" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
